            "review_title": "Review at Pin Wei",
            "review_text": "Nhi\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam3 contributions\n0\nFirst try of Singapore cake at Pin Wei\nMar 2026 • Friends\nI visited Pin Wei one afternoon and found the experience pretty good. Located in the center of District 1, close to the market, it is easy to find. The Singaporean cake here is different from the Vietnamese cake I eat, the skin of the cake is soft, super smooth and the sauce part has its own taste, eating quite charming. The menu topping is also diverse so going in groups will be easy to call many tastes to try. Lots of room, many tables, parking space. Overall, it’s a good place to try if you want to eat something weird but still easy to eat.\nRead more\nTranslated from Vietnamese\nShow original\nWritten June 15, 2026",
