            "review_title": "Review at Pin Wei",
            "review_text": "Trần Trâm A\n4 contributions\n0\nMichelin Guide–Recognized Singapore-Style Rice Rolls in District 1\nJan 2026 • Couples\nI tried this place because I noticed a lot of foreign tourists dining here, and it turned out to be a pretty interesting experience. The rice rolls are Singapore-style, so the wrapper is quite different from Vietnamese bánh cuốn — very thin, soft, and smooth. The sauce really stands out, as it’s made with a special in-house recipe that gives it a unique and well-balanced flavor. The menu offers a good variety with around seven main rice roll flavors and different toppings to choose from. The restaurant is conveniently located in the heart of District 1, right next to Ben Thanh Market. The space is airy with plenty of seating, and parking is spacious and convenient. They also offer free delivery within District 1 when ordering five main dishes or more, which is a nice bonus.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 23, 2026",
